# Local development only. Copy to .env.local.
#
# Deployed builds do not read this file. Their values come from .env.staging or
# .env.production — both in git — and which one is decided by which Dockerfile
# the trigger builds: Dockerfile.staging or Dockerfile.production. Adding an
# environment means a .env.<name>, a Dockerfile.<name>, and a trigger pointed at
# it; no code changes.
#
# .env.local wins over all of them, so what you set here only affects you.

# Which backend to call. Left unset, `npm run dev` falls back to the STAGING
# backend (see src/lib/api/client.ts), which is usually what you want when
# working on the UI alone. Point it at the backend repo running on this machine
# to work on both at once.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Which Supabase project signs users in — the same value as SUPABASE_URL in
# OJT-system-BE/.env. Staging and production are separate Supabase projects, so
# this decides whose auth.users you are authenticated against.
#
# Not a secret: it is the address the browser is sent to and it ships in every
# build.
#
# The origin you serve from must also be on that project's redirect allow-list,
# or Google sends people back with an error.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
